cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use speedread or its evals in your work, please cite it as below."
title: "speedread: token-efficient code search and navigation for AI coding agents"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Green
    given-names: Brennen
repository-code: "https://github.com/brennengreen/speedread"
url: "https://github.com/brennengreen/speedread"
license: MIT
version: 0.1.0
date-released: "2026-09-26"
abstract: >-
  speedread is an MCP server and CLI that gives AI coding agents the part of a
  codebase a question needs, within a token budget: the function around each
  search hit, a large file's skeleton, a symbol's callers and implementations,
  or only what changed since the last read. In its evals (one model, one
  harness), it cut input tokens by 35% on code questions and by 57% on
  relationship questions; every trial and transcript is in the repository.
keywords:
  - model context protocol
  - coding agents
  - code search
  - code navigation
  - tree-sitter
  - context engineering
